  "behavior": [
    "Typed Sequence stores one actual BaseSequence. Native links, size, endpoints, allocator and lookup cache are authoritative; no detached mirror or indexed Vec traversal remains.",
    "Insertion, cursor insertion, removal, ranges, reverse, exchange, split, same-allocator splice and clear dispatch to actual raw base operations. Move transfers actual cache/base and owners.",
    "Shared Value and mutable ChangeValue update native cache with synchronized field-only writes. Shared allocator and item references survive cache updates.",
    "The Vec is an unordered allocation owner registry using swap_remove, never the traversal order. Destruction follows actual native links.",
    "Safe double-ended iterators project only values from live links and bound remaining yields to prevent duplicate mutable references.",
    "Sequence and HSequence Send/Sync, shared/mutable iterator Send/Sync, Sequence<PhantomPinned> Unpin and readonly unwind traits are preserved by compile assertions.",
    "Node deallocation uses original allocator/layout and an unwind guard because allocator-api2 0.4.0 Box destruction does not deallocate after an item destructor panics.",
    "Canonical metadata resets on clear unwind. Partial range deletion retains safe survivors and reclaims detached owner records on clear."
  ],
