  "remaining_gaps": [
    "An unordered Vec allocation-owner registry remains; its extra allocation footprint and linear owner lookup are not native allocation/performance parity.",
    "SequenceBaseAccess is a Rust synchronization guard, not full native const BaseSequence reference equivalence. Drop before cache-reading operations or another base_access call; same-thread reentry can deadlock. Structural reads remain usable while held.",
    "Safe mutable BaseSequence access is not exposed because it could violate typed node ownership. Explicit unsafe raw cursor operations retain validity obligations.",
    "Native different-allocator insertion with index greater than size dereferences an invalid find result and crashed an exploratory probe. This undefined branch is excluded from transition generation; Rust retains checked-index behavior.",
    "Rust destructor panic cleanup is a safety extension, not a claim about C++ throwing destructor equivalence.",
    "Generic C++ copy/assignment effects still require corresponding Rust Clone/clone_from implementations and explicit self-assignment adapters.",
    "Declaration/compiler body binding and whole-class completeness remain unclaimed."
  ]
